      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey im trying to integrate this stripe api for my side project but im getting a 402 error on the payment intent creation even though i know the card is good. what are the common reasons for a 402 and how should i go about checking my request payload to see if im missing something?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The 402 error, also known as a \"Payment Required\" error, is a common issue when integrating Stripe's payment gateway. It's likely that your request payload is missing a required parameter, which is causing Stripe to reject the payment intent creation. You can start by checking the Stripe documentation for the specific payment intent creation endpoint you're using.\n\nOne way to approach this is to compare your request payload to the Stripe API documentation. For example, when creating a payment intent, you'll need to provide the `amount` parameter, which specifies the amount of the payment in cents. Make sure you're including this parameter in your request payload.\n\nIt's also possible that the `currency` parameter is missing or incorrect. Stripe requires a valid currency code in the `currency` parameter. You can check the Stripe API documentation to see what currency codes are supported.\n\nAnother common issue is that the `payment_method_types` parameter is missing or empty. This parameter specifies the types of payment methods that can be used to make the payment. You'll need to include this parameter in your request payload, specifying the type of payment method you're using (e.g. `card`).\n\nTo help you debug the issue, I'd recommend using Stripe's API debugging tools",
